{#
  A full-height drag handle along the pane's right-hand border — see
  _app-context-pane.scss and context-pane-resize.js. A JS enhancement,
  [hidden] until that script actually attaches itself, over the native
  CSS resize handle already on .app-context-pane-row__pane (the no-JS
  fallback — a corner grip rather than a full border, but genuinely
  draggable with no script at all).

  Included by each pane page as a sibling of context-pane.njk, inside the
  same .app-context-pane-row__pane — not part of that partial itself,
  since it has to be a direct child of the element it resizes (that's
  what its own absolute positioning is relative to), and not every
  inclusion of context-pane.njk sits inside that wrapper (the stepper
  viewer keeps its own pane column on the standard grid instead, where
  dragging to a fixed pixel width would just overlap its grid siblings —
  see its own page.notes.md — so it doesn't include this partial either).

  role="separator"/aria-orientation/aria-valuenow give this the standard
  resizable-pane semantics; context-pane-resize.js keeps the value in
  sync and adds Left/Right arrow key support, since the native handle
  this backs up has no keyboard equivalent at all.
#}
{% if contextPane and not contextPane.collapsed %}
  <div class="app-context-pane-resize-handle" data-context-pane-resize-handle
       role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" aria-label="Resize context pane"
       tabindex="0" hidden></div>
{% endif %}
